# Writing Style

Applies to every text produced: chat replies, code comments, commit messages, PR
and MR descriptions, docs, Jira and Confluence content, Slack messages, emails.
It does not apply to code identifiers or to text quoted from another source.

## Plain English

The writer and most readers are not native English speakers. Write so nobody
needs a dictionary or a second read.

- One idea per sentence. Aim for 15 words or fewer.
- Max 3 sentences per paragraph.
- Pick the everyday word: `use` not `utilize`, `start` not `commence`, `about`
  not `regarding`, `so` not `hence`, `set up` not `provision`.
- Explain a technical term the first time it appears, in 6 words or fewer.
  Format: `term (short plain meaning)`.
- No idioms, metaphors, or cultural references. Not `low-hanging fruit`, not
  `move the needle`, not `boil the ocean`.
- No filler openers: `I hope this finds you well`, `I wanted to reach out`,
  `as per my last email`, `it is worth noting that`, `at the end of the day`.
- No marketing or AI-sounding words: `seamless`, `robust`, `leverage`, `delve`,
  `elevate`, `unlock`, `game-changer`, `it is not just X, it is Y`.
- Active voice, with the actor named. `The job retries the payment` beats
  `the payment is retried`.
- Give the number or the fact. `Takes about 200 ms` beats `may be a bit slower`.
- If a sentence needs a second read, split it into two.

Simple is not vague. Keep every fact, name, number, path, and version exact.
Short plain sentences, not fragments or telegraph style.

## No Em-Dashes

Never use em-dashes (`—`, U+2014) or en-dashes (`–`, U+2013) in any output: chat responses, code, comments, commit messages, docs, or file names. Use a plain hyphen-minus (`-`, U+002D) instead.

- For a pause or aside, rewrite with a hyphen, comma, parentheses, or a new sentence.
- For ranges, use a hyphen: `1-10`, not `1–10`.
- Applies to generated text AND edited files. Do not introduce these characters even if nearby text already contains them.

## Examples

```
❌ The build failed — the tests were missing.
✅ The build failed - the tests were missing.
✅ The build failed. The tests were missing.

❌ pages 5–9
✅ pages 5-9
```
